  {"date": "2014-12-31", "venue": "American Airlines Arena", "city": "Miami", "state": "FL", "gap": 11, "set": "2", "jamchart": true, "jam": "-&gt; from &quot;Theme&quot;, this &quot;Cities&quot; jam starts with some nice staccato work from Trey, passes through a Manteca-like section, and settles into the 3.0 Type II bliss zone.", "out": ">", "prev": "Theme from the Bottom", "in": "->", "next": "Chalk Dust Torture", "nb": 1},
  {"date": "2015-08-12", "venue": "The Mann Center for the Performing Arts", "city": "Philadelphia", "state": "PA", "gap": 19, "set": "1", "jamchart": true, "jam": "Trey's Echoplex leads the second straight solid &quot;Cities&quot; to some extended between-verses jamming, before the whole band picks up where he left off and explores a pulsing, minor mode space before the 'plex is left behind for a more straight-ahead jam that eventually fades out.", "prev": "Sample in a Jar", "next": "Stash", "nb": 1},
  {"date": "2015-08-22", "venue": "Watkins Glen International", "city": "Watkins Glen", "state": "NY", "gap": 5, "set": "3", "times": 2, "jamchart": true, "jam": "Another strong and typically funky \"Cities\" -> \"Mind Left Body Jam\" sandwich.", "out": "->", "prev": "Possum", "in": ">", "next": "Mind Left Body Jam", "nb": 1},
  {"date": "2016-01-16", "venue": "Barcel\u00f3 Maya Beach", "city": "Riviera Maya", "state": "Quintana Roo", "gap": 10, "set": "1", "jamchart": true, "jam": "After a stretch of perfunctory versions, &quot;Cities&quot; has now gone four for its last four. A laid back tropical vibe yields to a stormy, foreboding jam, before the sun peeks through the clouds and the -&gt; Light grows brighter.", "out": "->", "prev": "Rift", "next": "Light", "nb": 1},
  {"date": "2016-07-01", "venue": "Saratoga Performing Arts Center", "city": "Saratoga Springs", "state": "NY", "gap": 8, "set": "1", "prev": "NICU", "next": "David Bowie", "nb": 1},
  {"date": "2016-07-08", "venue": "Xfinity Center", "city": "Mansfield", "state": "MA", "gap": 4, "set": "1", "jamchart": true, "jam": "Early technical issues, a Brian Brown introduction, and a guitar switch do nothing to deter the band from taking &quot;Cities&quot; on a journey across the globe. Some strong but typical jamming leads to more instruments switching and the jam evolves / devolves into highly percussive near free-form jazz.", "note": "Trey broke a string and switched guitars mid-song, also introducing his guitar tech, Brian Brown. Trey then switched to Marimba Lumina and Mike played Trey's guitar.", "prev": "Fuego", "next": "Space Oddity", "nb": 1},
