  {"date": "2018-12-29", "venue": "Madison Square Garden", "city": "New York", "state": "NY", "gap": 6, "set": "1", "prev": "46 Days", "in": ">", "next": "Corinna", "nb": 1},
  {"date": "2019-06-26", "venue": "Darling's Waterfront Pavilion", "city": "Bangor", "state": "ME", "gap": 16, "set": "2", "jamchart": true, "jam": "-> out of a superb \"Fuego\". Gets deliciously, almost heavy-metal sludgy dark right out of the gate, Mike and Fish really powering this gruesomeness. Fish snaps into a wickedly danceable beat which the band rides for all it's worth (nearly swerving into \"Sand\" at one point), before they swing into a new key and pull out a sick -> into \"The Final Hurrah\". A wonderful jam.", "out": "->", "prev": "Fuego", "in": "->", "next": "The Final Hurrah", "nb": 1},
  {"date": "2019-12-01", "venue": "Nassau Veterans Memorial Coliseum", "city": "Uniondale", "state": "NY", "gap": 18, "set": "2", "out": ">", "prev": "Down with Disease", "in": "->", "next": "Carini", "nb": 1},
  {"date": "2021-09-01", "venue": "Shoreline Amphitheatre", "city": "Mountain View", "state": "CA", "gap": 32, "set": "1", "jamchart": true, "jam": "The band moves into a more driving version of the usual \"Cities\" jam, thanks to Fishman, before Trey makes the move into a brief bit of major key bliss, and then takes the jam into smoother and more relaxed waters. A very nice first set jam, with a wonderful -> into \"Passing Through\".", "out": "->", "prev": "The Wedge", "next": "Passing Through", "nb": 1},
  {"date": "2021-10-22", "venue": "Ak-Chin Pavilion", "city": "Phoenix", "state": "AZ", "gap": 9, "set": "2", "out": ">", "prev": "A Life Beyond The Dream", "next": "Harry Hood", "nb": 1},
  {"date": "2022-07-19", "venue": "TD Pavilion at the Mann", "city": "Philadelphia", "state": "PA", "gap": 28, "set": "2", "out": "->", "prev": "Tweezer", "in": "->", "next": "Tweezer", "nb": 1},
  {"date": "2022-08-05", "venue": "Atlantic City Beach", "city": "Atlantic City", "state": "NJ", "gap": 12, "set": "1", "out": ">", "prev": "Sigma Oasis", "in": "->", "next": "More", "nb": 1},
  {"date": "2023-04-23", "venue": "Hollywood Bowl", "city": "Hollywood", "state": "CA", "gap": 26, "set": "1", "jamchart": true, "jam": "This first set delight comes out the gate with swingin' swagger. Trey locks \nthe band into Bmin to escape the confines of \"Cities\" proper and the band\ndevelops an incredibly cohesive, melodic, effect-drenched boogie down. \nAfter the 12 minute mark, the music takes a hazy, cinematic turn towards\npatient psychedelia. This then develops into a gorgeous, technicolor \ndreamscape that crescendos towards anthemic territory before > \"Tube.\"", "out": ">", "prev": "Divided Sky", "next": "Tube", "nb": 1},
  {"date": "2023-07-21", "venue": "The Pavilion at Star Lake", "city": "Burgettstown", "state": "PA", "gap": 8, "set": "2", "out": "->", "prev": "David Bowie", "next": "Fuego", "nb": 1},
  {"date": "2023-07-28", "venue": "Madison Square Garden", "city": "New York", "state": "NY", "gap": 5, "set": "1", "jamchart": true, "jam": "Big Red's love affair with The Big Apple, coupled with his renewed interest in jamming \"Cities,\" yields a whole lotta good points. Chill playing ushers in fantastic, truly rhythmic improvisation, Trey's strumming offering a shimmery, warm, almost shoegaze feel - and, most importantly, room for the entire band to breathe. Play pulses until just after the 8:00 mark, when Trey takes a really great lead, which he builds into patterned play that bursts with a celebratory vibe. A nod to Trey's old home place, indeed.", "note": "Lyrics changed to \"find the best city to live in\" and \"I found myself a city to live in.\"", "prev": "A Wave of Hope", "next": "The Old Home Place", "nb": 1},
  {"date": "2023-10-07", "venue": "Bridgestone Arena", "city": "Nashville", "state": "TN", "gap": 14, "set": "2", "jamchart": true, "jam": "The \"Music City\" inspires another big 2023 version of \"Cities\". Mike's fat synth bass carves out the initial funky path. Trey and Page dial in the murk in response, crossing through some vague \"MLB\"-isms on the way to a \nmajor mode shift. The music turns on a dime toward celebratory fare, but retains some of its spacious-ness, as Trey alternates between clean melodic phrasing and long echoed notes. Play then cools back towards da \nfunk and -> \"Llama\".", "out": "->", "prev": "Everything's Right", "in": "->", "next": "Llama", "nb": 1},
  {"date": "2024-07-26", "venue": "Alpine Valley Music Theatre", "city": "East Troy", "state": "WI", "gap": 24, "set": "1", "out": ">", "prev": "Llama", "next": "Ya Mar", "nb": 1},
  {"date": "2024-08-10", "venue": "Bethel Woods Center for the Arts", "city": "Bethel", "state": "NY", "gap": 11, "set": "1", "out": ">", "prev": "Weigh", "next": "Run Like an Antelope", "nb": 1},
  {"date": "2024-08-29", "venue": "Dick's Sporting Goods Park", "city": "Commerce City", "state": "CO", "gap": 6, "set": "1", "jamchart": true, "jam": "Summer '24 Phish truly blurs the line between \"average-great\" and notable. Perhaps a case in point, here. Precision play from the jump before, come the 6:00 mark, Trey unleashes a series of savage licks. The band truly wakes, each adding \"parts\" informing this great sum. Play coasts before Trey finds a great melodic (pick a tease) riff, which Page mimics. A true Dick's harbinger.", "out": ">", "next": "Down with Disease", "first": 1, "nb": 1},
  {"date": "2025-01-29", "venue": "Moon Palace", "city": "Cancun", "state": "Quintana Roo", "gap": 11, "set": "2", "jamchart": true, "jam": "Things build slowly at first as Trey and Page politely occupy the same tonal space. Mike and Fish, by contrast, are driven and focused throughout. Trey eventually finds firm footing and digs his heels into more rocking and rif laden territory, and with the help of Page, now on piano, they push the improv to a satisfying peak and return.", "out": ">", "prev": "Set Your Soul Free", "in": ">", "next": "Light", "nb": 1},
  {"date": "2025-04-20", "venue": "Moda Center", "city": "Portland", "state": "OR", "gap": 6, "set": "1", "out": "->", "prev": "The Moma Dance", "in": ">", "next": "Plasma", "nb": 1},
  {"date": "2025-06-27", "venue": "Moody Center", "city": "Austin", "state": "TX", "gap": 10, "set": "1", "jamchart": true, "jam": "> from \"Mike's Song\", play is fluid, almost languid, great bass and drums accented by Trey's liquid tone and Page, who twice 'sprays' synth across the stage. Following a really cool line, listen for the locked-in audience (5:45) response before Trey, and the jam, takes off. What follows is Phish at its finest, post-21 refinement, perfect unrushed balance, improv that rolls, roils, and, refreshingly, doesn't build to peak but, rather, smartly draws to a close.", "prev": "Mike's Song", "in": ">", "next": "Divided Sky", "nb": 1},
  {"date": "2025-07-23", "venue": "Forest Hills Stadium", "city": "Forest Hills", "state": "NY", "gap": 15, "set": "1", "jamchart": true, "jam": "Sticky clav-led funk rock is shaped by Trey's melodic bluesy riffing to start. Major key tonalities then take over, and the band rides out this bliss-rock feel until the \"Cities\" chords come back in to conclude the affair.", "note": "With added lyrics.", "prev": "Theme from the Bottom", "next": "Divided Sky", "nb": 1},
  {"date": "2025-09-13", "venue": "Coca-Cola Amphitheater", "city": "Birmingham", "state": "AL", "gap": 5, "set": "1", "jamchart": true, "jam": "Birmingham proper finally got a \"Cities\" and it was one to remember. Coming as the second song of the night, the band shows they're ready to let loose. Mike leads the jam early and the slow funk gradually picks up tempo. The jam winds its way to a more contemplative space before > into \"Sample\".", "out": ">", "prev": "Back on the Train", "next": "Sample in a Jar", "nb": 1},
  {"date": "2026-04-25", "venue": "Sphere", "city": "Las Vegas", "state": "NV", "gap": 20, "set": "1", "jamchart": true, "jam": "Cosmopolitan jam that stays fairly close to home rhythmically but departs melodically under Trey\u2019s lead, brightening and decorating the neighborhood with a brisk and buoyant optimism and a gentle uplift before returning to the song to conclude.", "prev": "Axilla (Part II)", "in": ">", "next": "Horn", "nb": 1},
